  "title": "Laurie C NDE 4241",
  "date": "'6 th may, 1984'",
  "content": "I remember seeing those car lights [was going to say on our side of the road], then total blackness. I thought to myself, I'm dead. So, this is death. I wasn't at all frightened, and when I thought about how I should be frightened, a wave of pure love washed through my being. I felt totally at peace and very safe, and love was in me and around me everywhere. I was calm and had no thought of the accident. No pain, just absolute peace. I remember thinking that I could still think and noticed how alert I was. Then a voice said to me, ‘do you want to stay or do you want to go back?’ The clarity of that sentence was amazing, and as clear as it was, I didn't know if it was male or female. I said, ‘I've just had a baby [4 1/2 months old] and the next thing I knew I was on the side of the road with someone holding me and I was gasping for breath. Before the accident, as I was getting into the car, a voice said, also with extreme clarity, ‘car accident’, that's all. Just those two words. I looked around but no one was there. It was the most fantastic experience and I feel very grateful for it. I no longer feel any fear about death and now know when others die that they’re ok and their lives have not ended. It was a very enlightening and rewarding experience and it has changed the way I think and feel. The experience is always with me every day and the clarity of it is still there, and I would even say the love that comes with it grows stronger.",
